& [WorkerProofIdentity] is specification evidence rather than canonical or implementation authority
  + [purpose] is close the language-design gaps that otherwise let syntax, labels, compiler targets, provider output, or graph proximity silently acquire meaning or authority
  + [scope] is grammar profile, SemanticIR validation, types, effects, modules, transformations, targets, diagnostics, compatibility, and conformance
  + [status] is ready_for_manager_review_and_SMTC_SJS_consumption
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent
  + [physical_storage_authority] is deferred

& [CompilerPipelineIdentity] is one meaning with many checked projections
  + [source_input] is exact SourceGeneration plus declared LanguageProfile and RoleDeclarationShape
  + [front_end] is parse then role closure then semantic analysis
  + [semantic_center] is one canonical SemanticIR whose identities and contracts retain source correspondence
  + [back_end] is one or more TargetProfile lowerings through the common TargetABI
  + [result] is a PackageFamily containing target artifacts, diagnostics, proofs, correspondence, and loss records
  = must: distinguish accepted source, resolved meaning, optimized meaning, lowered artifact, admitted package, and executed effect
  - never: use successful parsing, compilation, signature metadata, or target generation as evidence that an artifact may execute

& [LanguageProfileContract] bounds syntax before meaning
  + [profile_uuid] is stable identity
  + [profile_version] is immutable semantic version
  + [surface_family] is verbose_SOP, condensed_SOP, machine_SOP, or explicitly_registered_extension
  + [grammar_digest] binds the exact grammar generation
  + [lexical_rules] define tokens, whitespace, comments, escaping, quoting, identifiers, literals, and source locations
  + [syntactic_rules] define declarations, clauses, relations, directives, expressions, blocks, contracts, modules, and program regions
  + [desugaring_rules] map supported surface conveniences into explicit SemanticIR constructors
  + [role_requirements] declare which DocumentRole and RegionRole forms the profile accepts
  + [feature_set] lists required and optional semantic features
  + [unsupported_form_policy] is preserve_with_diagnostic or reject_under_requested_compilation
  + [compatibility_range] declares eligible source and dependency versions
  = must: make profile selection explicit and digest-bound
  = must: map verbose, condensed, and machine forms with equal meaning to the same canonical SemanticIR
  - never: infer document role, effect authority, trust, or executable admission from grammatical shape

& [ParsingBoundary] separates recognition from judgment
  + [parser_input] is bytes, encoding, source identity, generation digest, and LanguageProfile
  + [parser_output] is SyntaxTree, SourceMap, ParseDiagnosticSet, and unsupported extension records
  + [parser_success] means only that the selected grammar recognized the requested region
  + [recovery_node] preserves skipped or malformed source without inventing executable meaning
  + [unknown_extension_node] preserves an unrecognized extension under exact span and namespace
  = must: retain comments, quotations, delimiters, and raw spans when their loss could change meaning or provenance
  - never: treat parser recovery, token resemblance, indentation, imperative mood, or keyword presence as semantic admission

& [CanonicalSemanticDataSet] defines compiler identities
  + [CompilationUnit] binds source generation, selected profile, role declarations, requested entries, dependencies, targets, and authority request
  + [SourceGeneration] binds document UUID, immutable content digest, encoding, version, provenance, and supersession relation
  + [DocumentRoleDeclaration] binds artifact role, admission class, lowering disposition, execution disposition, effect disposition, and authority scope
  + [RegionDeclaration] binds stable region UUID, exact source span, region role, parent region, and referenced dependencies
  + [SyntaxTree] is profile-specific recognized structure with complete source mapping
  + [ResolvedBinding] binds one reference occurrence to exact semantic identity, version, namespace, context, and source declaration
  + [SemanticType] declares kind, value domain, relation constraints, qualifiers, and allowed operations
  + [RelationSignature] declares participant roles, direction, arity, cardinality, temporal scope, and inference regime
  + [EffectSignature] declares effect kind, resource, authority, scope, reversibility, compensation, observation, and fault behavior
  + [ModuleManifest] binds exports, imports, dependencies, roles, initialization, profiles, capabilities, and digests
  + [TargetProfile] binds target identity, ABI version, supported feature set, required proofs, loss policy, and artifact schema
  + [TargetCapability] is one explicitly versioned semantic feature or effect facility supported by a target
  + [LossRecord] binds one source or IR identity to omitted, approximated, nondeterministic, provider-dependent, or unsupported target behavior
  + [Diagnostic] binds code, stage, severity, source spans, semantic identities, expected state, actual state, repair options, and authority consequence
  + [ConformanceCase] binds source forms, expected SemanticIR, target expectations, proofs, diagnostics, and negative assertions
  + [CorrespondenceManifest] maps source identities through SemanticIR identities to every emitted target artifact region
  + [PackageFamily] binds all projections of one SemanticIR root without asserting equivalence beyond supplied proofs

& [StaticSemanticPassOrder] is deterministic and fail-closed
  + [pass_01_role_and_region_closure] validates document role, region role, mixed-document boundaries, admission class, and requested entry extent
  + [pass_02_source_and_dependency_integrity] validates source generation, digest, profile, dependency version, freshness, supersession, and provenance
  + [pass_03_name_context_and_import_resolution] resolves namespaces, identities, aliases, context bindings, exports, imports, and ambiguity
  + [pass_04_kind_type_and_relation_validation] validates semantic kinds, value domains, relation signatures, cardinalities, direction, and qualifiers
  + [pass_05_contract_completeness] validates purpose, inputs, preconditions, assumptions, invariants, permissions, obligations, prohibitions, outputs, faults, and termination
  + [pass_06_state_transition_and_control_validation] validates state ownership, legal transitions, branch closure, loops, yields, returns, stops, and unreachable obligations
  + [pass_07_authority_capability_and_effect_validation] validates eligible authority, capability provenance, effect rows, resource scopes, consent, reversibility, and compensation
  + [pass_08_target_capability_and_loss_validation] validates selected TargetProfiles, feature coverage, approximation policy, nondeterminism, provider dependence, and exact fallback
  + [pass_09_termination_and_budget_validation] validates bounded iteration, recursion, context, time, tokens, memory, tools, retries, and external operations
  + [pass_10_proof_obligation_formation] emits exact obligations for equivalence, compatibility, effect safety, target correspondence, and runtime admission
  = must: execute passes in order because each later pass consumes identities and constraints established by earlier passes
  = must: retain all non-cascading diagnostics while preventing later passes from treating invalid earlier results as resolved facts
  - never: optimize, lower, package, sign, or execute a CompilationUnit with blocking diagnostics

& [SemanticKindSystem] distinguishes language roles
  + [TermKind] names or denotes a concept under explicit context
  + [ValueKind] carries a typed literal or computed value
  + [RelationKind] relates typed participants through a RelationSignature
  + [DeclarationKind] introduces an identity, binding, rule, form, or environment member
  + [JudgmentKind] records proposed, supported, accepted, rejected, or unresolved semantic determination
  + [ContractKind] constrains eligibility, behavior, authority, evidence, effects, faults, and completion
  + [OperationKind] is a typed semantic transform without automatic execution authority
  + [ProgramKind] composes admitted operations under one complete SemanticContract
  + [ResultKind] records value, state delta, proposal, proof, observation, or emitted artifact
  + [FaultKind] records typed failure, rejected admission, or unresolved condition
  = must: attach context, provenance, authority status, judgment status, purity, effect set, temporal scope, and provider dependence as explicit qualifiers
  - never: infer subtype, equivalence, authority, or truth from label similarity, embedding distance, graph proximity, or shared target representation alone

& [TypeCompatibility] preserves semantic identity
  + [identity_rule] exact semantic identity is compatible with itself under allowed version and context scope
  + [declared_subtype_rule] subtype use requires an explicit, non-contradictory relation within the selected inference regime
  + [parameter_rule] generic parameters retain variance and constraints declared by their constructor
  + [union_rule] selection from alternatives requires evidence for the chosen member
  + [intersection_rule] use requires satisfaction of every member constraint
  + [unknown_rule] unknown is preserved and cannot satisfy a required concrete type without an authorized narrowing judgment
  + [conflict_rule] contradictory bindings produce a blocking diagnostic rather than arbitrary precedence
  + [conversion_rule] every non-identity conversion is explicit, source-mapped, and classified as exact, lossy, or provider-dependent

& [EffectSystem] makes action boundaries inspectable
  + [PureEffect] reads only immutable admitted values and emits a value or judgment without state mutation
  + [AttentionEffect] widens, narrows, holds, releases, admits, excludes, preserves, peeks, or returns model-visible attention under a declared frame
  + [EpistemicEffect] proposes, supports, challenges, accepts, rejects, or defers a judgment without converting it into external fact
  + [MemoryReadEffect] reads an authorized memory scope
  + [MemoryWriteEffect] proposes or commits a bounded memory mutation according to separate authority
  + [DatabaseReadEffect] queries a bounded database scope
  + [DatabaseWriteEffect] proposes or commits a bounded database transaction
  + [FileEffect] reads, creates, edits, moves, or removes exact filesystem resources under declared capability
  + [GitEffect] observes or changes exact repository state through typed operations
  + [ToolEffect] invokes one registered tool contract with typed request and response
  + [ProviderEffect] invokes an external or neural provider and records model, configuration, nondeterminism, and evidence limits
  + [UserAuthorizationEffect] requests or consumes explicit user authority without widening it
  + [ExternalEffect] communicates with or changes an external system or person under explicit scope
  + [effect_row] is the closed or explicitly extensible set of effects an operation may perform
  + [effect_instance] binds kind, target resource, operation, eligible authority, granted scope, reversibility, compensation, observation, and budget
  = must: distinguish propose, authorize, commit, and observe phases
  = must: require read and write capabilities separately
  = must: preserve denied, failed, partial, compensated, and unobserved outcomes as distinct states
  - never: let compilation, inference, provider generation, or a read capability imply write or commit authority

& [ModuleSystem] binds reusable meaning without authority leakage
  + [module_identity] is UUID plus immutable version and content digest
  + [namespace] is explicit and collision-checked
  + [exports] list exact identities, roles, types, effects, contracts, and target features made available
  + [imports] select exact module identity, compatible version set, symbols, aliases, and expected digests
  + [dependency_graph] must resolve to one versioned graph with recorded conflicts
  + [cycle_policy] permits only declared cycle-safe definition groups and rejects initialization or effect cycles
  + [initialization] is absent by default and, when present, is an explicit admitted program entry with its own contract
  + [target_declarations] state compatible targets without forcing every consumer to select them
  + [authority_rule] imported definitions and contracts constrain the importer but imported authority does not transitively widen the importing program
  + [private_identity_rule] non-exported identity remains unavailable even if discoverable in storage
  + [supersession_rule] newer versions do not silently replace an exact imported generation

& [StandardLibraryBoundary] keeps the core small and versionable
  + [language_intrinsic] is limited to semantic identity, context, source mapping, contract structure, typed state, control, effect declaration, fault, and result constructors required to express the language
  + [standard_module] is an ordinary exact versioned module distributed with the language profile and admitted through normal dependency checks
  + [faculty_module] packages Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Weaver, Planner, or other faculty behavior as explicit definitions, contracts, and programs rather than hidden compiler behavior
  + [target_library] provides one target-specific implementation behind the CommonTargetABI and cannot redefine canonical semantics
  + [provider_adapter] provides typed neural or external-provider requests and responses without becoming a language intrinsic
  + [platform_adapter] provides filesystem, git, database, calendar, process, network, UI, or hardware effects under explicit capability
  + [bootstrap_minimum] is the smallest independently trusted intrinsic set needed to parse, validate, serialize, and compare the canonical fixture
  = must: version, digest, test, and import standard, faculty, target, provider, and platform modules explicitly
  - never: promote convenient host behavior into an implicit semantic or authority rule

& [SemanticIRObligations] make the semantic center authoritative
  + [canonical_identity] every IR node has stable semantic identity within the exact compilation
  + [source_correspondence] every node maps to source spans or an explicit generated-node derivation
  + [role_correspondence] every node retains source document and region roles
  + [contract_correspondence] every operation, program, and entry point binds its governing contract
  + [type_and_effect_correspondence] every executable node has resolved type and effect signatures
  + [authority_correspondence] every effectful node binds requested authority without asserting runtime grant
  + [target_neutrality] IR meaning does not depend on one backend's incidental representation
  + [uncertainty_preservation] unresolved, ambiguous, contested, approximate, and provider-dependent states remain typed
  + [deterministic_serialization] canonical serialization produces the same semantic root for equivalent accepted input under the same profile and compiler version

& [OptimizationLawSet] forbids semantic laundering
  + [eligibility] an optimization names the exact input IR, rewrite law, assumptions, affected effects, and target scope
  + [equivalence] exact rewrites require a discharged semantic-equivalence proof obligation
  + [approximation] non-equivalent rewrites are target approximations and require a LossRecord plus policy admission
  + [effect_order] non-commutative effects retain program order
  + [authority_preservation] rewrites cannot add, widen, merge, conceal, or erase authority requirements
  + [provenance_preservation] rewrites retain correspondence to all contributing source identities
  + [fault_preservation] rewrites preserve specified fault conditions and observation distinctions
  + [contract_preservation] rewritten programs continue to satisfy all preconditions, invariants, obligations, prohibitions, outputs, and termination bounds
  + [rollback] optimized and unoptimized artifacts remain traceably selectable for differential proof

& [CommonTargetABI] is the stable compiler-backend seam
  + [abi_request] contains CompilerIdentity, SemanticIRRoot, SourceMap, SemanticContractSet, ModuleClosure, TargetProfile, TargetCapabilitySet, AuthorityRequest, ProofPolicy, and Budget
  + [abi_response] contains TargetArtifactSet, CorrespondenceManifest, DiagnosticSet, ProofArtifactSet, LossRecordSet, ProviderDependencySet, NondeterminismRecord, and TargetManifest
  + [support_result] is exact_supported, supported_with_declared_approximation, provider_dependent, or unsupported
  + [refusal_rule] unsupported required features, prohibited loss, missing proof, missing capability, or incompatible ABI version produce a blocking response with no executable artifact
  + [identity_rule] emitted artifacts bind the same SemanticIR root and selected TargetProfile digest
  + [reproducibility_rule] deterministic targets bind toolchain and configuration; nondeterministic targets bind seeds when available and always declare residual nondeterminism
  + [admission_rule] target generation never substitutes for trusted-package or runtime admission

& [RuntimeABI] separates built artifacts from admitted execution
  + [runtime_request] contains PackageFamilyIdentity, requested entry point, typed inputs, exact source and SemanticIR roots, target artifact identity, runtime profile, granted capability set, eligible authority evidence, effect budget, and trace policy
  + [runtime_response] contains typed result or fault, transition trace, proposed and committed effects, observations, residual uncertainty, resource use, and reentry state
  + [admission_check] revalidates package signature, scope, validity, revocation, dependency closure, target compatibility, entry contract, capabilities, authority, and budgets at time of use
  + [effect_broker] mediates every non-pure effect and distinguishes requested, authorized, committed, denied, failed, compensated, and observed states
  + [provider_broker] treats neural and external provider returns as typed evidence or proposals according to the exact target contract
  + [replay_boundary] records deterministic inputs and declared nondeterminism sufficient to reconstruct or explain the run within the target's stated guarantee
  + [debug_surface] exposes source, SemanticIR, target, state, contract, effect, diagnostic, and trace identities without permitting debugger inspection to mutate them
  + [termination_result] distinguishes normal return, explicit stop, budget exhaustion, cancellation, blocked effect, fault, and unresolved judgment
  - never: let a runtime load an artifact, dependency, capability, or authority outside the admitted package and request scope

& [TargetProjectionContracts] specialize the ABI without changing source meaning
  + [SOP_X_exact] emits deterministic exact executable fabric and must reject unsupported semantic behavior rather than approximate it
  + [SOP_N_neural] emits training, routing, prompting, retrieval, gating, or model-blueprint artifacts whose outputs remain typed proposals
  + [SOP_H_hybrid] emits exact orchestration around bounded neural proposals with explicit fallback, challenge, and refusal routes
  + [SOP_A_attention] emits bounded model-visible attention frames and query directives without source or effect authority
  + [SOP_D_data] emits schemas, indexes, projections, query plans, and provenance mappings while retaining identity and role boundaries
  + [SOP_T_tool] emits typed tool or service interfaces with explicit request, response, fault, capability, and side-effect contracts
  + [SOP_W_workflow] emits dependency graphs, worker claims, completion proofs, and admission checkpoints
  + [SOP_F_FPGA] emits either an interpreter-layer artifact or native hardware fabric only under a hardware profile and correspondence proof
  + [SOP_I_interface] emits human or machine interfaces that explain or manipulate admitted semantics without promoting display text to authority

& [DiagnosticContract] makes failure actionable and non-deceptive
  + [diagnostic_code] is stable within compiler generation
  + [stage] identifies parse, role, dependency, resolve, kind, type, relation, contract, state, control, authority, effect, target, budget, proof, package, or admission
  + [severity] is information, warning, blocking_error, security_fault, or integrity_fault
  + [location_set] includes all relevant source and generated spans
  + [semantic_identity_set] names affected terms, relations, contracts, operations, modules, effects, and targets
  + [expected] states the exact required condition
  + [actual] states observed input without silently normalizing it
  + [repair_set] supplies zero or more bounded, non-authoritative repair candidates
  + [authority_consequence] is none, target_blocked, package_blocked, execution_blocked, effect_blocked, or quarantine
  + [causal_chain] distinguishes primary faults from dependent diagnostics
  = must: make unknown, ambiguous, contradictory, unsupported, stale, unauthorized, lossy, and provider-dependent conditions distinct
  - never: auto-apply a repair that changes meaning, role, authority, effect, or source generation

& [CompatibilityContract] supports evolution without silent drift
  + [source_compatibility] asks whether a source generation is accepted by a named LanguageProfile
  + [semantic_compatibility] asks whether old and new SemanticIR satisfy declared observational obligations
  + [module_compatibility] asks whether exports, imports, types, effects, contracts, and authority expectations remain valid
  + [target_compatibility] asks whether the target ABI and capability set preserve required semantics
  + [package_compatibility] asks whether trust, dependency, scope, validity, and revocation remain admissible
  + [migration_plan] is required for incompatible changes and names source transform, proof, rollback, and preserved prior generation
  + [legacy_default] is preserve and diagnose, not reinterpret and execute
  + [signature_rule] a prior signature retains only its original scope and never inherits new compiler-purpose authority

& [ConformanceSystem] proves the language contract through independent observations
  + [canonical_fixture] contains equivalent verbose, condensed, and machine SOP source forms
  + [front_end_assertion] requires those forms to resolve to the same canonical SemanticIR root under the same profile
  + [role_assertion] requires instruction-shaped data, proof, narrative, policy, and profile artifacts to remain non-executable
  + [type_effect_assertion] requires all executable nodes to have resolved types, closed or explicitly extensible effect rows, and authority requests
  + [module_assertion] requires exact imports, no authority widening, and deterministic conflict diagnostics
  + [target_assertion] requires each backend to declare exact support, loss, nondeterminism, provider dependence, and correspondence
  + [cross_target_assertion] compares target observations only within the equivalence boundary each target claims
  + [negative_fixture] exercises unknown role, mixed boundary leak, ambiguous binding, invalid subtype, hidden effect, import conflict, illegal cycle, unsupported target feature, prohibited optimization, and signature-as-authority
  + [implementation_independence] requires at least one conformance consumer that does not reuse the compiler path being tested for its expected result
  + [proof_bundle] binds fixture source, profiles, compiler, SemanticIR, targets, diagnostics, observations, and result digest

& [MinimumCrossTargetFixture] is the first implementation proof after separate implementation authorization
  + [program] is a pure typed semantic program with one definition, one data value, one relation, one bounded inference, one condition, and one emitted result
  + [source_forms] are verbose, condensed, and machine equivalents
  + [SOP_X_result] is deterministic exact result and trace
  + [SOP_N_result] is a neural blueprint or provider request whose answer is explicitly proposal_only
  + [SOP_H_result] is exact admission of a neural proposal followed by deterministic validation or refusal
  + [negative_result] includes an instruction-shaped quotation that remains data and an undeclared write effect that blocks compilation
  + [proof_goal] is semantic-root equality for surface forms and explicit correspondence, loss, and authority boundaries across targets
  + [current_authority] is specification_only; implementation awaits a later claimed worker slice

& [AcceptanceCriteria] are sufficient for SMTC purpose processing
  + [accept_01] parser success cannot establish program role or execution eligibility
  + [accept_02] role and region closure is the first semantic validation pass
  + [accept_03] every admitted program operation resolves kind, type, contract, effect, and authority request
  + [accept_04] imports cannot widen authority and effectful module cycles are rejected
  + [accept_05] exact, neural, and hybrid backends share one ABI while declaring materially different proof and loss requirements
  + [accept_06] optimization cannot hide effects, authority, faults, provenance, or approximation
  + [accept_07] every emitted target region maps back to SemanticIR and source identities
  + [accept_08] unsupported features fail closed instead of receiving guessed lowering
  + [accept_09] diagnostics distinguish uncertainty, contradiction, incompatibility, loss, and authority failure
  + [accept_10] canonical fixtures test equal surface meanings, cross-target boundaries, and explicit negative cases

& [NegativeCriteria] expose invalid compiler behavior
  + [reject_01] executable status inferred from syntax, filename, directory, prose mood, signature presence, or target selection
  + [reject_02] graph distance or embedding similarity used as an undeclared subtype or identity rule
  + [reject_03] provider output treated as fact, exact semantics, permission, or effect authority
  + [reject_04] read authority reused as write authority
  + [reject_05] optimization reorders non-commutative effects or erases source correspondence
  + [reject_06] module import silently selects a newer dependency or transitively imports authority
  + [reject_07] target backend emits an executable artifact after reporting unsupported required semantics
  + [reject_08] legacy source is migrated in place or prior signature scope is silently expanded

& [DeferredPhysicalDesign] preserves the proper design order
  + [deferred] concrete parser generator, Rust data layout, database schema, index selection, cache design, binary encoding, neural architecture, FPGA instruction set, provider choice, and deployment topology
  + [reason] is those are physical implementations of the conceptual and logical contracts above and require separate implementation slices after canonical authority
  + [allowed_next_design] is SMTC SJS integration, registry binding, justification, canonical authority, and a bounded future fixture authorization
  - never: mistake a proposed physical representation for the language's semantic identity

& [WorkerConclusion] completes WS-CTPR-003
  + [settled_expression] is SOP source is parsed under an explicit profile, validated through ordered role-first static semantics into one source-mapped SemanticIR, and projected through a proof-carrying target ABI that refuses undeclared loss or authority
  + [support_delta] is grammar boundary, compiler data identities, semantic passes, kind/type/effect/module systems, optimizer laws, target ABI, diagnostics, compatibility, fixtures, and negative criteria are formed
  + [requirement_delta] is SMTC canonical processing must bind these contracts while leaving physical implementation and runtime execution unauthorized
  + [remaining_uncertainty] is exact surface grammar and physical schemas are intentionally profile and implementation artifacts, not missing purpose semantics
  + [next_worker] is WS-CTPR-004 complete SMTC explosion, refinement, data design, constraints, pruning, exhaustion, justification, registry, canonical specification, and valid bounded SJS signature
  + [canonical_authority] is absent_until_SMTC-SJS-01
